-- I25-bare: main.mdk with ONE variable changed — the import form. The standalone, the
-- prelude interface it collides with, the receiver and the call are all identical; only
-- the spelling the occurrence is written under differs.
--
-- `import amod.{shrink}` DOES bind bare `shrink` in this module, so `shrink 5` IS an S1
-- importer-shadow occurrence, S2's importer arm finds the live prelude `impl Arbitrary
-- Int` at the receiver's head, and dispatch is what conformance requires: `[0, 2]`,
-- `Arbitrary.shrink`'s prelude default at 5. This is the FORK-1 control for main.mdk —
-- a fix that gave the alias-qualified occurrence back to the standalone by widening the
-- rule to every spelling would move this cell too, and the everyday `import map`
-- pattern with it. IT MUST NOT MOVE.
--
-- Measured UNCHANGED across #1684's fix: run and the built binary both printed `[0, 2]`
-- before it and both print `[0, 2]` after. That the two engines already AGREED here is
-- exactly why this row's value is derived from the clause rather than captured.
import amod.{shrink}

main = println (shrink 5)
